dialect protocol
protocol tiff.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.tiff
start record

# P2-FG2: REAL binary op frame, replacing F6's `print_op().into_bytes()` text-as-binary shortcut
# (`../../🦀️component.rs`'s old `OpBinary::encode_op` -- see that file's `#region OpCodecs` for
# the upgraded implementation). `TiffMutation` is a genuine data-carrying enum whose `SetTag`/
# `SetSnapshot`/`InsertIfd` variants embed `TiffValues` (a 12-variant data-carrying enum) directly
# or recursively through `TiffIfd`/`TiffSnapshot` -- no `DslField` impl exists or can exist for a
# data-carrying enum (confirmed live, F6's own recon: adding `#[derive(dsl::DslOps)]` fails
# `DslField is not satisfied` for `TiffValues`, same root cause `../../🔺️diff/🦀️component.rs`'s
# own doc comment documents for `TiffDiff`), so the generic `format u8 | ordinal varint | record
# body` layout genuinely does not fit. Handcrafted instead: `format u8` (`store::pack_rt::
# OP_BINARY_FORMAT` convention) + `tag u8` (the `TiffMutation` variant ordinal, same 0-7 ordering
# as `print_tiff_mutation`'s own keyword match) as two REAL fixed fields, then the variant's own
# index/ifd/tag/kind/values payload as one opaque trailing `bytes` chain.
#
# The recursive/variant-shaped payload itself is real varint-framed binary
# (`enc_snapshot_bin`/`enc_ifd_bin`/`enc_values_bin` in the same `🦀️component.rs`, reusing
# `store::pack_rt::write_varint_u64`/`store::ByteReader`) -- NOT re-modeled field-by-field here
# because a repeated per-entry-varying-shape RECORD collection (`TiffIfd`'s tag entries, each
# entry's `TiffValues` shape varying by field-type) is the `protocol-array-of-records` mechanism
# gap (§5) -- confirmed unchanged since M2, hit by every stdio pilot's own recursive/collection-
# shaped mutation payload. This is the same honest-boundary treatment the plan itself prescribes
# for a compressed payload segment -- opaque at the protocol layer, genuinely structured (and
# round-trip-tested) at the Rust layer.
framing record
header fixed 2
field format u8
field tag u8
chain payload bytes
